Third-party software bundled with Abotica

Abotica itself is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (see LICENSE). The
sandbox image (Dockerfile, target `sandbox`, built as abotica-sandbox:latest) bundles the software
below, each under its own license. The license files that ship with each package stay in the image,
at the paths given.

Base image and system packages
------------------------------

- Debian 13 (trixie) and the Debian packages installed in the image, including the libraries
  Chromium needs. Licenses: one per package, in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.
- Node.js 24 (official node:24-trixie-slim image). License: MIT, with the licenses of its
  bundled dependencies at https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/main/LICENSE (the official image
  does not include that file).
- uv and uvx (Astral), Composer, yq (Mike Farah): copied in as binaries. Licenses: uv is
  MIT OR Apache-2.0; Composer is MIT; yq is MIT.

